From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: ExplorerBrowser answers like Windows (2016)

shell32: ExplorerBrowser answers like Windows (2016)

From Wine's conformance tests (todo_wine blocks that record Windows):
SendControlMsg, SetStatusTextSB, ContextSensitiveHelp, EnableModelessSB,
SetToolbarItems and OnViewWindowActive answer S_OK; the control's window
has WS_CLIPCHILDREN; IInputObject activates and tracks the focus of the
shell view and hands keys to it; the browser is an IServiceProvider and an
IConnectionPointContainer (IExplorerBrowserEvents). The shell view handles
the file list's keys in TranslateAccelerator and EnableModeless succeeds.
